    // graph coloring, the minimum number of colors (layers) equals the size 
    // of the maximum clique in the interval overlap graph, which for intervals 
    // is the maximum number of intervals that all contain a common point.

    // For segments with integer endpoints, the "interior" points are the 
    // half-integer points between consecutive integers. A segment [i, j] 
    // (with i < j) contains the half-integer point k + 0.5 if and only if 
    // i <= k and j >= k+1, i.e., i <= k < j.

